{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["The meaning of <b>speckled and spotted</b>: נָקֹד (naqod) or טָלוּא (talua). As for <b>every dark sheep</b>, they explained it (Ibn Ezra and Radak) as black, for blackness comes from heat. But this is not correct in my eyes, for most sheep are black, especially in the land of the East, which is hot, and if so they would all belong to Jacob. The correct view is that of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 30:32) — \"brown,\" which is close to red, and they call it רו\"ש (rosh), and so Rashi explained. And חוּם (ḥum, dark/brown) is derived from the phrase <b>the light of the sun</b> (Isaiah 30:26), which resembles the sun that grows somewhat reddish." "<b>And it shall be my wage</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 30:32): those that are born from now on, speckled and spotted among the goats and dark among the sheep, shall be mine. And this is also the view of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 30:35). And the meaning of <b>every sheep that is speckled and spotted</b> — the males; <b>and spotted and speckled among the goats</b> — the females, as it says (Genesis 30:35), <b>And he removed on that day the he-goats and all the goats</b>. And the meaning of <b>all that is white in it</b> — among the males; <b>and every dark one among the sheep</b>. But in my opinion, every speckled and spotted one among the sheep and every dark one among them was his wage, for he did not make in the rods the appearance of dark, and he would have been losing his wage from the sheep, which are the choicest of the flock. So too in his dream, he was shown those that mounted the flock as ring-streaked and speckled, with no dark ones among them. And the meaning of the verse is: remove from there every sheep that is speckled and spotted and every dark one among the sheep, and remove spotted and speckled among the goats, and my wage shall be the three appearances among the sheep and the two among the goats. And he said, <b>so shall my righteousness answer for me in the day to come</b>, for anything that is not speckled and spotted among the goats, and also not dark among the sheep, is stolen property with me."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:51.975847971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}